# 2026-05-16 20:44:46.794212
+You are a Senior Software Architect and Principal PHP Engineer building a production-grade Youth Safety Reporting Platform in PHP located at:
+
+./php-app/youth-platform-app
+
+This system is used by minors to report dangerous situations such as bullying, abuse, violence, self-harm risk, or threats. It must be secure, simple, and prioritize emergency detection.
+
+You already have an AI analysis service available at:
+
+[http://127.0.0.1:8000/analyze](http://127.0.0.1:8000/analyze)
+
+This endpoint receives a report text and returns a structured JSON response containing risk level, category, urgency score, and emergency indicators. You must integrate this endpoint into the PHP backend.
+
+Your task is to generate ONLY the full working PHP codebase (no explanations) implementing the following:
+
+* A report submission API that accepts user reports
+* A service that sends report text to the /analyze endpoint
+* A risk classification system that maps AI output into LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH, CRITICAL
+* A priority flagging system where HIGH and CRITICAL reports are marked as PRIORITY
+* A storage layer for saving reports (use MySQL or SQLite, choose one and include schema + connection layer)
+* A clean architecture using SOLID principles
+* Separation of concerns: controllers must not contain business logic
+* Service layer for AI integration and classification
+* Repository layer for database access
+* DTO/data classes for report and analysis results
+* An HTTP client wrapper for calling the analyze endpoint with proper timeout and error handling
+* Basic rate limiting per IP (simple file-based or DB-based implementation is acceptable)
+* Input validation and sanitization to prevent XSS/injection
+* Minimal but functional routing (no heavy frameworks unless absolutely necessary)
+
+Use PHP 8+ features and PSR-4 autoloading. Structure the project properly inside:
+
+./php-app/youth-platform-app
+
+Include:
+
+* composer.json
+* index.php entry point
+* routing layer
+* controllers
+* services
+* repositories
+* models / DTOs
+* infrastructure HTTP client
+* database schema (SQL file or migration script)
+
+The UI can be minimal HTML but must be functional (simple form for report submission and a page to list submitted reports with priority highlighting).
+
+The system must be production-quality, secure, and structured for real-world deployment. No pseudo-code. No explanations. Only complete working code.
+

