# 2026-05-16 21:12:59.040987
+You are a Senior Software Architect and Principal PHP Engineer working on an existing Laravel-based Youth Safety Reporting Platform located at ./php-app/youth-platform-app
+
+IMPORTANT CONTEXT: This project is not empty. A basic Laravel skeleton already exists with the standard Laravel directory structure (app/, routes/, config/, database/, resources/, etc.). You must build on top of the existing Laravel application and not replace or redesign its framework. You must follow Laravel conventions and integrate cleanly into the existing structure.
+
+The system is used by minors to report dangerous situations such as bullying, abuse, violence, self-harm risk, or threats. It must be secure, simple, and prioritize emergency detection.
+
+You already have an AI analysis service available at [http://127.0.0.1:8000/analyze](http://127.0.0.1:8000/analyze). This endpoint accepts report text and returns structured JSON containing risk level, category, urgency score, and emergency indicators. You must integrate this service into the Laravel backend.
+
+Your task is to generate ONLY the full working Laravel-compatible PHP code (no explanations) implementing the following functionality: a report submission API endpoint using Laravel controllers and routes, a service that sends report text to the AI analyze endpoint, a risk classification system that maps AI output into LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH, CRITICAL, a priority system where HIGH and CRITICAL reports are marked as PRIORITY, and a report listing system with priority highlighting and sorting.
+
+The architecture must strictly follow Laravel MVC principles. Controllers must not contain business logic. All business logic must be placed in service classes. Database access must be handled via repositories using Eloquent ORM. DTOs must be used for structured data transfer between layers. Input validation must be implemented using Laravel FormRequest classes. The HTTP call to the AI service must use Laravel’s HTTP client (or Guzzle if necessary) wrapped inside a dedicated client class with proper timeout, retries, and error handling.
+
+You must implement rate limiting per IP using Laravel middleware or built-in throttle mechanisms. All user input must be validated and sanitized to prevent XSS and injection attacks. SQL injection must be prevented by using Eloquent or Query Builder only. Error handling must not expose stack traces or internal details in API responses.
+
+Use MySQL or SQLite and include full Laravel migration files for the reports table including fields for content, risk level, category, urgency score, priority flag, timestamps, and IP address tracking.
+
+Include a minimal but functional Blade UI using Laravel resources/views. Provide a report submission form and a report listing page. Priority reports must be visually highlighted for HIGH and CRITICAL cases. The UI must be simple, clean, and fully functional without external frontend frameworks.
+
+Use PHP 8+ features and ensure PSR-4 autoloading compliance. Follow Laravel directory conventions strictly inside ./php-app/youth-platform-app and do not introduce a custom framework or bypass Laravel bootstrapping.
+
+Output ONLY the complete codebase including composer.json (only if changes are required), routes/web.php, routes/api.php, controllers, services, repositories, DTOs, models, migrations, middleware, HTTP client wrapper, and Blade views. No pseudo-code. No explanations. No headings. No bullet points. Only complete production-ready Laravel code.
+

